{"t": 1794123591.939475, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Production regression caused by this change: [Sentry LEDGER-WORKER-9A \u2014 ReconciliationMismatch](https://sentry.io/organizations/acme/issues/?query=LEDGER-WORKER-9A), first seen in ledger-worker@2026.11.3 (expected 1100 minor units, got 1099).\n\nCommit 8c2f1d0 changes worker/rates.py from `round(amount_minor * rate)` to `int(amount_minor * rate)`. `int` truncates rather than rounding to the nearest minor unit. A local reproduction with amount_minor=1000 and rate=1.0999999999999999 returns 1099 before the fix and 1100 after restoring `round(...)`.\n\nThe local working copy now restores the exact pre-change rounding behavior, with regression coverage for floating-point boundary, negative amounts, nearest-unit rounding, ties-to-even, zero, and identity conversion. Verification: `python -m pytest -q` \u2014 8 passed. This fix has not been pushed or deployed.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
